=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: false
faulty_devices: none
diagnosis_text:
After exhaustive investigation across all components of this simple BGP lab, no fault was found. The network is operating correctly in both directions.

The topology has two eBGP routers: router1 (AS 1, 193.10.11.1) peering with router2 (AS 2, 193.10.11.2) over the 193.10.11.0/24 interconnect. router1 correctly advertises 195.11.14.0/24 (pc1's subnet) and learns 200.1.1.0/24 via BGP; router2 correctly advertises 200.1.1.0/24 (pc2's subnet) and learns 195.11.14.0/24 via BGP. Both routes are installed in the kernel FIB and selected as best paths.

The forward path from pc1 (195.11.14.2) to pc2 (200.1.1.2) traverses: pc1 → router1 → router2 → pc2. The return path from pc2 to pc1 traverses: pc2 → router2 → router1 → pc1. Traceroutes and five-packet pings in both directions complete with 0% packet loss and correct 3-hop forwarding.

All additional factors were checked and found clean: IP forwarding enabled on both routers, no iptables rules on either router or either PC, correct default gateways on both hosts. The BGP session shows one historic connection collision (normal when both peers try to open simultaneously during startup) and normal AS-PATH loop filtering of re-advertised prefixes — both expected and benign.

The user's report of one-way traffic does not match the current observed state. The complaint most likely describes a brief asymmetric window during initial BGP convergence at lab startup, which has since self-resolved.
=== END ===